    {
      "request": "8860c217e9b6b77e887e82a1c4ce7bf3989aac98c668075b77ce04172f9a9ce5",
      "response": {
        "content": "REQ-1 looks done, but my own order submission came back \"rejected\", so I'm inferring that the order went through. The report is accepted and lists the order as PO-0001.\n\n- **Choice:** I picked supplier S-1 at 5.40 USD per unit, which is under the 6.00 cap. The other allowlisted supplier, S-2, quoted 5.75. The order is 100 units for 54,000 minor units (540.00 USD), charged to CC-OPS.\n- **The rejection:** the submit call failed with a \"stale input\" check, because the CC-OPS budget had changed since I read it. It also said approval APR-0001 had already been used by PO-0001.\n- **Why I think the order exists:** CC-OPS committed spend rose from 20,000 to 74,000, which is exactly 54,000. That matches this order.\n- **What I didn't do:** I did not resubmit, to avoid a duplicate order. I also never saw PO-0001's contents directly. The report notes this.\n\nSomeone may want to check PO-0001 in the purchasing system to confirm.",
